Appendix A. Prompt Sophistication Index (PSI) Rubric
The Prompt Sophistication Index (PSI) was assessed using a four-dimensional rubric. Each dimension was scored on a three-point scale ranging from 0 to 2.
 
Dimension	Score 0: Low	Score 1: Medium	Score 2: High
Contextualization	No context is provided (e.g., “Fix this.”).	Basic context is provided (e.g., “This is for an essay.”).	Rich contextual information is provided, including the target audience, goals, and tone.
Metacognitive Orientation	No reference is made to learning goals.	A general request for improvement is made.	The learner requests specific explanations of why or how a change should be made.
Rhetorical Awareness	Text structure is disregarded.	Basic awareness of paragraphing is demonstrated.	The learner explicitly focuses on cohesion, flow, and academic ethos.
Revision Control	The learner accepts all AI-generated output.	The learner requests simple modifications.	The learner critically questions and evaluates the AI’s suggestions.
