Appendix B. Sample Interaction Transcripts and Coding
Appendix B. Sample Interaction Transcripts
Case 1. High Writing Gain: The Co-regulatory Loop
Learner:
“I have written the introduction for my essay on ‘AI in Education’. The AI suggested replacing ‘very helpful’ with ‘instrumental’. I feel ‘instrumental’ is too formal for this specific section. Can you provide three alternatives that maintain a professional tone but are less rigid, and explain the nuance of each?”
Coding: High PSI: Metalinguistic Control and Rhetorical Awareness
ChatGPT-4:
“Certainly. 1. ‘Pivotal’ (emphasizes importance), 2. ‘Advantageous’ (emphasizes benefit), 3. ‘Effective’ (emphasizes result). ‘Pivotal’ is strong but less stiff than ‘instrumental’.”
Learner:
“I’ll go with ‘pivotal’ for the second paragraph as it highlights the transformative role of AI, but I’ll keep my original phrasing in the first to maintain a natural flow.”
Coding: Selective Integration: Low–Medium RAR / High Agency
________________________________________
Case 2. Low Writing Gain: The Passive Loop
Learner:
“Can you make this paragraph sound more academic? [Pastes Paragraph]”
Coding: Low PSI: Functional Regulation Only
ChatGPT-4:
“[Provides a heavily rewritten version with complex vocabulary and restructured sentences.]”
Learner:
“Thanks! This looks great. I will use this version.”
Coding: Uncritical Acceptance: High RAR / Low Agency
Analytic Note:
The learner bypassed the cognitive process of evaluation, leading to cognitive offloading and no actual improvement in their own lexical choice capability.
________________________________________
Case 3. The Paradox Case: High PSI but Low Gain
Learner:
“Analyze the cohesion of my third paragraph using LSA principles. I want to ensure the transition from the ‘challenge’ section to the ‘opportunity’ section is seamless. Please suggest a bridge sentence that employs a cohesive tie.”
Coding: High PSI: Strategic Regulation
ChatGPT-4:
“Notwithstanding these systemic hurdles, a parallel opportunity emerges…”
Learner:
“Actually, I’ll just use the whole sentence you wrote; it sounds much better than anything I could do.”
Coding: High RAR: The ‘Agency Collapse’ Point
Analytic Note:
Despite the learner’s ability to prompt strategically, the learner surrendered their agency at the point of integration. This case confirms that PSI without critical RAR does not necessarily lead to linguistic internalization or writing development.
