Appendix C. Computational Metrics and Software Details
The computational measures and statistical procedures were implemented as follows:
Lexical Diversity:
Lexical diversity was calculated using the Lex diversity package in R version 4.2.1. The selected measure was the Measure of Textual Lexical Diversity (MTLD).
Semantic Alignment:
Semantic alignment was processed using Coh-Metrix 4.0, standardized for academic corpora. The analysis focused on Latent Semantic Analysis (LSA).
Linear Mixed-Effects Model Analysis:
The longitudinal analyses were conducted in R using the lme4 and lmerTest packages. Restricted Maximum Likelihood (REML) was used for the estimation of variance components.
Socio-Technical Setup:
All learner–AI interactions were conducted using ChatGPT-4 (GPT-4-1106-preview) to ensure consistency in model temperature and response quality.
